          hints: [
            'Which part of the request carries the most risk: the style of a named person, or the promise?',
            'A good reply separates what you can say (what you read) from what you cannot (a guarantee).',
            'One option changes the prompt and reads the terms. Another only changes the prompt.',
          ],
          explanation: 'The strongest response reduces the risk you can control (do not target one living person\'s style) and is honest about what you cannot promise. A guarantee or a blanket refusal both claim more certainty than anyone has.',
